{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791036471,"nonce":"dC1SzprPUvhSYU9YLmwPfNu8kzE=","title":"Creating a signal inside a derived or effect closure deadlocks","message":"`signal()` and `computed()` take `global_graph().lock()`. During a\nderived recompute or an effect flush that lock is already held on the\nsame thread, so a nested creation blocks forever.\n\nReads and writes already have in-flight paths: `IN_FLIGHT_GRAPH`\npublishes `*const ReactiveGraph`, reads go through it and record\nthemselves as dependencies, and writes are deferred. Creation has no\nsuch path.\n\nSolidJS allows it. The case that hits it is a lazily created signal whose\nfirst read happens inside a computed — a theme token created on first\naccess, say. Reported by the ashui session, which works around it by\ncreating its theme signals eagerly and now raises a clear error instead\nof hanging.\n\n\nWanted: a `signal()` usable while a closure is in flight, with the new\nsignal readable AND recorded as a dependency in that same evaluation.\n\nThe blocker is that the in-flight path yields `\u0026ReactiveGraph` while\n`create_signal` takes `\u0026mut self`. The fix that fits the existing design\nis interior mutability for `signals`, and `derived` for `computed()`.\nThe struct already does exactly this for everything else touched during\nan evaluation: `pending_effects`, `tracking`, `batch_depth`,\n`global_version` and `derived_dirty_buffer` are all `RefCell` or `Cell`.\nOnly the three `SlotMap`s need `\u0026mut`.\n\nAssessed as tractable, with caveats:\n\n- 14 sites touch `self.signals`. Each needs checking for a borrow held\n  across a call into user code.\n- The one place that calls user code, `(*compute)(self)` in\n  `get_derived`, passes `self` and holds no `signals` borrow, so the\n  obvious hazard is absent.\n- `create_signal(\u0026mut self)` becoming `(\u0026self)` is a loosening, so\n  existing callers keep compiling.\n- Reads in the same evaluation must see the new signal, which falls out\n  of inserting into the same storage rather than staging it elsewhere.\n\nThe risk is not the mechanism but the file: two RefCell-reentrancy bugs\nin this module were fixed within a day of writing this — 8f037c6, a\ncomputed read inside another computation, and 4375436, the Windows\n\"RefCell already borrowed\" panic. A borrow held one frame too long here\nturns a rare deadlock into a panic on a hot path, which is worse.\n\nNot urgent: ashui has a working error and an eager-creation workaround.","files":null}]}